PASS — finite Cursor and Grok Bot fields observed
$ codexbar cards --provider cursor --no-color
PASS — Cursor, Third Party, and Grok Bot labels observed

Privacy
- Fixture and transport tests use synthetic credentials, endpoints, and usage values.
- The user-supplied screenshot is retained verbatim at `../../cursor_fix.png` and visibly includes the account label and card values.
- Apart from that requested screenshot, live token, cookie, reset timestamp, identity, and usage values were omitted from this artifact.
- The real Cursor state database was read-only and unchanged.

Environment limits
- `make check` is not clean on Debian because its installer regression requires macOS AppleScript.
- `lint-linux` reaches the portable checks, then SwiftLint cannot load Debian SourceKit; no clean lint claim is made.
